preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: "Hendrick's Identity: an explicit formula and sharp minimum for a classical three-vortex collapse family"
  authors:
    - name: "Chaos"
      website: "https://github.com/SharpMeow"
  year: 2026
  month: 9
  url: "https://github.com/SharpMeow/GENChase/blob/main/IDENTITIES.md"
  repository-code: "https://github.com/SharpMeow/GENChase"
  abstract: >-
    Three point vortices with circulations (1, 1, -1/2) on the L=0 circle
    collapse self-similarly. Their dimensionless product of initial angular
    velocity and collapse time is omega_0 t_c = (2 - cos^2 theta) / sin(2 theta)
    >= sqrt(2), with equality uniquely at tan theta = 1/sqrt(2), a triangle
    of interior angles 22.5, 45, and 112.5 degrees. Independently derived
    in GENChase with AI assistance. Recorded here 2026-09-19; historical
    priority unconfirmed.
    Also referred to as Hendrick's law and Hendrick's Math. Cite as
    Hendrick's Identity.
  keywords:
    - Hendrick's Identity
    - Hendrick's law
    - Hendrick's Math
    - point vortex
    - self-similar collapse
    - Gröbli
    - Aref
